[| An individual is considered to be lawfully present in the United States ifhe or she: 1. Is a qualified non-citizen as defined in 8 U.S.C. 1641(b) and (c),

2. Is anon-citizen in a valid nonimmigrant status, as defined in 8 U.S.C. 1101(a)(15) or otherwise under the immigration laws (as defined in 8 U.S.C. 1101(a)(17));

3. Is a non-citizen who has been paroled into the United States in accordance with 8 U.S.C. 1182(d)(5) for Jess than 1 year, except for an individual paroled for prosecution, for deferred inspection or pending removal proceedings;

